{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/829504-plant-protean","id":829504,"title":"Plant Protean","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-13T18:51:06-08:00","id":829504,"title":"Plant Protean","content":"I liked the plant Animalism from the Gangrel book, I'd love to see an update as well as a version of it for Protean.<br /> <br /> I'll kick us off with a rough idea.<br /> <br /> Dryad's Steps:<br /> <br /> unlike protean the kindred can only sink into plants, instead of soil or rock, the kindred can travel through the root sytem and even jump into other plants for 1 viate per 10 yards (or up to 10 yards per dot ini viate) also while in a blank network the kindred can feed. Killing the plant in the process leaving a tree withered or an entire lawn brown.<br /> <br /> Aspect of the Mother: Just like protean 2 for reular protean, but more plant like appearnce <br /> <br /> Shape of the mother: first thoughts is shape into a plant but that seems worthless<br /> <br /> Greater Aspect: Same as 2<br /> <br /> 5: ???<br /> <br /> ideas??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T19:16:36-08:00","id":829517,"title":"","content":"In my game headcanon there is a Discipline called Genesis that is basically the Plant Discipline, from one of the Antediluvians that never Sired childer. Powers involving ghouling plants, plant shapeshifting, and higher level powers touching upon returning to the cycle of life, and drinking Sunlight as a tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T20:47:54-08:00","id":829545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/829504-plant-protean?p=829517#post829517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my game headcanon there is a Discipline called Genesis that is basically the Plant Discipline, from one of the Antediluvians that never Sired childer. Powers involving ghouling plants, plant shapeshifting, and higher level powers touching upon returning to the cycle of life, and drinking Sunlight as a tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like it. Care to share a write up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T20:50:22-08:00","id":829548,"title":"","content":"It was for Classic World of Darkness so it would have to be rejigged for Requiem and I don't have the notes anymore but I can work it from memory if need be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T04:35:24-08:00","id":829658,"title":"","content":"Movement powers are generally the providence of Celerity. If you want to make a &quot;Dryad's Step&quot; power, you'd probably be better off using Protean/Celerity than Animalism. Shadow Step, ala Khabit, is similar to what was suggested, and it uses Obfuscate/Celerity.<br /> <br /> While I love the theme of Rose and Thorn merit from the Gangrel book, Plants aren't exactly highly mobile, which makes using it with Animalism a bit strange. So, while communication with plants would be pretty awesome (we'd need rules for how long they remember stuff), ordering them to do something is kinda odd. You'd have to rewrite the Raise the Familiar power, Feral Infection power, and Summon the Hunt.<br /> <br /> I honestly think the biggest obsticle is that Cruac pretty much dominates the manipulate-plants stick. Even looking at other games for inspiration, we end up with growing plants in a wide area, nourishing fruits, entangling, spikey ground, tree walking, plant merging/form, and talking with plants as potential plant-themed powers. Encouraging growth is a Cruac style. Magic fruits are mandrake gardens, another CotC merit. Entangling and spiked ground are Cruac rituals - Hawthorn Barrier, Flower of Demeter and Thorned Snare*. Even the plant-themed <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Adroanzi bloodline </span></span>didn't have a lot of plant powers we could use for inspiration.<br /> <br /> If you absolutely wanted a plant themed power, I'd steal the above stuff from Cruac and put it in the following format:<br /> 1 - Talk with plants. Can ask about anything in an area of connected plants (ie what's going on in a given park, garden, forest, etc.)<br /> 2 - mandrakes you control can grapple<br /> 3 - Plants lash out at people at command, inflicting one Environmental Penalty of your choice, refluffed to come from plants instead of weather. Not all may apply in all circumstances.<br /> 4 - Bleed out and force plants to grow in direction you desire. May use with 2 and 3.<br /> 5 - Repeat Lord of the Land, but less animal control and more ability to use any of the lower powers at will anywhere in territory.<br /> <br /> Its not very pretty - this is only a rough outline of plant themed powers. Disciplines should all build upon the first dot, following a progression. This doesn't quite.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, merging with plants / plant form can easily be just reworked Protean levels. First dot power, merge with wood. Done. Second and Fourth dots we'd need some plant themed transformations. Bark skin is classic, as is floral scents. Third dot is to turn into a plant yourself, if necessary. Fifth dot is fine as is. Plant step is a Protean 1 / Celerity 2 devotion.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Thorned Snare was from the Blood Sorcery book, but the CotC book has Path of Thorns, which is effectively the same power. Hawthorn Barrier is from Bloodlines: the Chosen, and Flower of Demeter is from the Cotories book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-14-2016, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T05:10:56-08:00","id":829675,"title":"","content":"The Nburu discipline from Ancient Bloodlines (page 109-111) has a couple of powers that are noted as protean-like. The third dot lets you merge with a sufficiently large plant (generally a tree) and see out of any part of it. The fifth dot lets you teleport from one suitable plant to another.<br /> <br /> Let's start with tree merge for dot1, then for dot 2 you can shapeshift features of plants you've spent at least a day merged with.<br /> <br /> For dot 3 how about you can move any plant you're bonded with (suck blood through roots or whatever) and make it grow aspects you've absorbed and can replicate with dot 2.<br /> <br /> Then maybe have the fourth dot be jumping from tree to tree (and thus follow people who flee your wrath), and the fifth lets you spread across an entire forest and manipulate every tree in there as if you were merged with it.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe for the fifth dot we could call it a radius of [blood potency]... Miles? Miles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 02-14-2016, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T11:25:11-08:00","id":831901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/829504-plant-protean?p=829675#post829675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nburu discipline from Ancient Bloodlines (page 109-111) has a couple of powers that are noted as protean-like. The third dot lets you merge with a sufficiently large plant (generally a tree) and see out of any part of it. The fifth dot lets you teleport from one suitable plant to another.<br /> <br /> Let's start with tree merge for dot1, then for dot 2 you can shapeshift features of plants you've spent at least a day merged with.<br /> <br /> For dot 3 how about you can move any plant you're bonded with (suck blood through roots or whatever) and make it grow aspects you've absorbed and can replicate with dot 2.<br /> <br /> Then maybe have the fourth dot be jumping from tree to tree (and thus follow people who flee your wrath), and the fifth lets you spread across an entire forest and manipulate every tree in there as if you were merged with it.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe for the fifth dot we could call it a radius of [blood potency]... Miles? Miles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like a lot of this though as someone said above jumping through root system should be a devotion. Maybe when your in plant shape you don't take damage buy if the plant you're in is destroyed you return to your original shape and take half the damage equal to the structure of the plant and can't resume that shape for the night","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}